Sarcastically.

281
00:28:49,110 --> 00:28:52,270
Something like this will definitely help people take the club more seriously.

282
00:28:53,750 --> 00:28:55,150
Yeah, I thought so too.

283
00:28:56,050 --> 00:28:57,450
I flipped through the pages.

284
00:28:58,310 --> 00:29:01,150
Each member's poem is neatly printed on its own page.

285
00:29:01,530 --> 00:29:03,530
Giving it an almost professional feel.

286
00:29:03,690 --> 00:29:04,270
By the way!

287
00:29:04,990 --> 00:29:09,710
I was conflicted, actually, after last time, whether or not I even wanted to continue this game.

288
00:29:10,830 --> 00:29:12,330
But at this point, it's more...

289
00:29:12,330 --> 00:29:14,910
Like, I am not, like, completely in love with this at all.

290
00:29:14,910 --> 00:29:15,450
You know?

291
00:29:16,030 --> 00:29:19,790
Like, I feel like everything up to this point has been kinda...

292
00:29:21,450 --> 00:29:22,510
Like, not good.

293
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:23,390
You know what I mean?

294
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:26,430
Like, I don't wanna shit too much on it, but it's kinda not that great.

295
00:29:27,350 --> 00:29:29,330
And, at this point, I'm more like...

296
00:29:30,410 --> 00:29:31,650
It's a short game, right?

297
00:29:31,670 --> 00:29:33,190
I just kinda wanna see it to the end.

298
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:36,170
Also because people love it so much, so I'm kinda curious, you know?

299
00:29:36,610 --> 00:29:39,510
Like, maybe it'll win me over later, I don't know, I doubt it, but we'll see.

300
00:29:39,990 --> 00:29:41,130
Just wanted to put that up.

301
00:29:41,950 --> 00:29:46,470
I recognize Natsuki's and Yuri's poems from the ones they performed during our practice.

302
00:29:47,730 --> 00:29:48,570
What's this?

303
00:29:49,870 --> 00:29:51,670
I flipped to Sayori's poem.

304
00:29:52,850 --> 00:29:54,750
It's different from the one she practiced.

305
00:29:55,510 --> 00:29:56,050
Oh yeah?

306
00:29:56,650 --> 00:29:58,350
It's one that I haven't read before.

307
00:29:58,530 --> 00:29:59,670
Oh god, it's probably about me.

308
00:30:02,430 --> 00:30:03,790
Get out of my head.

309
00:30:06,650 --> 00:30:09,070
Okay, so Sayori is...

310
00:30:09,690 --> 00:30:10,670
Not doing too great.

311
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:15,790
Get out of my head before I do what I know is best for you.

312
00:30:16,370 --> 00:30:19,310
Get out of my head before I listen to everything she said to me.

313
00:30:19,770 --> 00:30:22,570
Get out of my head before I show you how much I love you.

314
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:25,550
Get out of my head before I finish writing this poem.

315
00:30:26,870 --> 00:30:28,570
But a poem is never actually finished.

316
00:30:28,810 --> 00:30:29,890
It just stops moving.

317
00:30:30,610 --> 00:30:31,050
Huh?

318
00:30:33,010 --> 00:30:34,310
I mean, she's talking to me.

319
00:30:34,430 --> 00:30:37,270
I don't know what the percentage sign is here, but...

320
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:39,650
It's like, I want you out of my head.

321
00:30:39,830 --> 00:30:40,570
What's that song?

322
00:30:41,690 --> 00:30:43,670
Out of my head, my head, my head, my head.

323
00:30:43,830 --> 00:30:44,930
Something about like, you know.

324
00:30:46,230 --> 00:30:47,250
There's a song like that.

325
00:30:47,590 --> 00:30:47,830
Ah!

326
00:30:49,210 --> 00:30:49,850
What's this?

327
00:30:50,930 --> 00:30:53,430
Reading the poem, I get a pit in my stomach.

328
00:30:54,730 --> 00:30:55,130
Oliver?

329
00:30:56,310 --> 00:30:56,950
What's wrong?

330
00:30:58,690 --> 00:30:59,810
Ah, nothing.

331
00:31:00,890 --> 00:31:04,290
This poem feels completely different from everything else Sayori's written.

332
00:31:04,570 --> 00:31:06,530
I can't wait to see her perform it.

333
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:09,310
I hope she's going to be verbatim saying everything.

334
00:31:10,010 --> 00:31:11,510
But more than that...

335
00:31:11,510 --> 00:31:12,490
I...

336
00:31:12,490 --> 00:31:13,870
I changed my mind.

337
00:31:14,810 --> 00:31:16,810
I'm gonna go get Sayori, so...

338
00:31:17,610 --> 00:31:18,030
Ah!

339
00:31:18,730 --> 00:31:19,570
Well, alright.

340
00:31:20,450 --> 00:31:21,910
Try not to take too long, okay?

341
00:31:22,990 --> 00:31:23,870
Ah, sure.

342
00:31:23,870 --> 00:31:25,610
I quickly leave the classroom.

343
00:31:26,830 --> 00:31:28,030
Don't strain yourself!

344
00:31:29,190 --> 00:31:30,330
I hear in the distance.

345
00:31:31,130 --> 00:31:32,770
Monica calls out that after me.

346
00:31:32,990 --> 00:31:34,710
I really butchered that one, didn't I?

347
00:31:35,070 --> 00:31:36,350
I quicken my pace.

348
00:31:36,890 --> 00:31:38,050
I like that sentence.

349
00:31:38,990 --> 00:31:40,110
What was I thinking?

350
00:31:40,930 --> 00:31:43,490
I should have tried a little bit harder for Sayori.

351
00:31:43,590 --> 00:31:44,190
No, I shouldn't.

352
00:31:45,130 --> 00:31:45,610
I...

353
00:31:45,610 --> 00:31:46,630
It's not the girl I want.

354
00:31:46,770 --> 00:31:47,390
I want Yuri.

355
00:31:48,330 --> 00:31:50,930
It's not a big deal to at least wait for her, or...

356
00:31:50,930 --> 00:31:52,030
help her wake up.

357
00:31:52,150 --> 00:31:52,510
What...

358
00:31:52,510 --> 00:31:53,210
Why?

359
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:57,790
Even the simple gesture of walking her to school makes her really happy.

360
00:31:59,170 --> 00:32:02,590
Besides, I told her yesterday that things will be the same as they always have been.

361
00:32:03,310 --> 00:32:05,650
That's all she needs, and what I want to give her.

362
00:32:07,450 --> 00:32:09,570
I reach Sayori's house and knock on the door.

363
00:32:10,370 --> 00:32:13,330
I don't expect an answer, since she's not picking up her phone either.

364
00:32:14,310 --> 00:32:16,310
I'm getting a really bad feeling about this.

365
00:32:16,910 --> 00:32:19,250
Like yesterday, I opened the door and let myself in.

366
00:32:22,050 --> 00:32:22,530
Sayori?

367
00:32:24,090 --> 00:32:25,710
She really is a heavy sleeper.

368
00:32:26,590 --> 00:32:27,910
Yeah, keep telling yourself that.

369
00:32:28,670 --> 00:32:29,610
I swallow.

370
00:32:30,810 --> 00:32:33,110
I can't believe I ended up doing this after all.

371
00:32:36,020 --> 00:32:37,740
Waking her up in her own house?

372
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:40,780
Isn't that more like something a boyfriend would do?

373
00:32:41,180 --> 00:32:43,420
Also, just walking into her house?

374
00:32:43,980 --> 00:32:45,600
It's kinda fucked up, isn't it?

375
00:32:46,620 --> 00:32:48,040
In any case...

376
00:32:48,460 --> 00:32:49,480
It just feels right.

377
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:50,780
Does it?

378
00:32:51,700 --> 00:32:53,800
Outside Sayori's room, I knock on her door.

379
00:32:55,300 --> 00:32:55,780
Sayori?

380
00:32:57,180 --> 00:32:58,220
Wake up, dummy!

381
00:32:59,220 --> 00:33:00,280
There's no response.

382
00:33:01,820 --> 00:33:04,160
I really didn't want to have to enter her room like this.

383
00:33:04,380 --> 00:33:07,820
You can't just enter someone's room like this, let alone house!

384
00:33:08,960 --> 00:33:10,660
Isn't it kind of a breach of privacy?

385
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:11,280
Yes!

386
00:33:11,660 --> 00:33:12,520
It is!

387
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,780
But she really leaves me no choice.

388
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:17,700
I gently open the door.

389
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:18,940
Oh!

390
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:20,780
Jesus fucking Christ, that scared me!

391
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:25,040
I fucking figured something like this would happen.

392
00:33:27,140 --> 00:33:28,560
Wow, they're actually showing that.

393
00:33:29,500 --> 00:33:30,560
What the hell?

394
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:36,320
An exception has occurred.

395
00:33:41,190 --> 00:33:41,910
Wait, what?

396
00:33:41,990 --> 00:33:43,010
Are we inside a simulation?

397
00:33:44,430 --> 00:33:45,190
Nothing's real.

398
00:33:46,890 --> 00:33:48,170
See traceback for details?

399
00:33:48,390 --> 00:33:49,330
How do I open the traceback?

400
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:51,830
What the hell?

401
00:33:52,670 --> 00:33:54,530
Okay, at least we confirmed the music is working.

402
00:33:56,390 --> 00:33:57,730
What the hell?!

403
00:33:58,910 --> 00:33:59,990
Is this a nightmare?

404
00:34:00,630 --> 00:34:01,630
Oh, is it a dream?

405
00:34:02,870 --> 00:34:03,810
It has to be.

406
00:34:04,670 --> 00:34:05,550
This isn't real.

407
00:34:06,750 --> 00:34:07,690
Yeah, that's what I said.

408
00:34:07,750 --> 00:34:08,290
It's fake.

409
00:34:09,070 --> 00:34:10,390
There's no way this can be real.

410
00:34:11,730 --> 00:34:12,850
Sayori wouldn't do this.

411
00:34:12,950 --> 00:34:13,850
I don't know about that.

412
00:34:14,830 --> 00:34:16,610
But the fact that they're showing all this...

413
00:34:16,610 --> 00:34:18,850
Everything was normal up until a few days ago.

414
00:34:20,330 --> 00:34:22,750
That's why I can't believe what my eyes are showing me.

415
00:34:25,010 --> 00:34:26,930
I suppressed the urge to vomit.

416
00:34:28,190 --> 00:34:29,190
Just yesterday.

417
00:34:29,870 --> 00:34:32,090
I told Sayori I would be there for her.

418
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:36,370
I told her I know what's best, and that everything will be okay.

419
00:34:37,330 --> 00:34:38,230
Then why?

420
00:34:39,270 --> 00:34:40,610
Why would she do this?

421
00:34:41,530 --> 00:34:43,030
How could I be so helpless?

422
00:34:43,870 --> 00:34:45,050
What did I do wrong?

423
00:34:45,690 --> 00:34:46,210
Nothing.

424
00:34:46,990 --> 00:34:48,290
Turning down her confession?

425
00:34:50,770 --> 00:34:52,830
That has to have been what pushed her over the edge.

426
00:34:54,010 --> 00:34:56,390
Her agonized scream still echoes in my ears.

427
00:34:57,950 --> 00:35:00,370
Why did I do that to her when she needed me the most?

428
00:35:01,870 --> 00:35:03,350
Well, what should I have done?

429
00:35:05,850 --> 00:35:08,070
Giving her false hope is the worst thing I could have done.

430
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:10,570
Why was I so selfish?

431
00:35:11,090 --> 00:35:11,870
You were not.

432
00:35:12,930 --> 00:35:13,990
It's not your fault.

433
00:35:14,850 --> 00:35:18,090
My swarming thoughts keep telling me everything I could have done to prevent this.

434
00:35:19,950 --> 00:35:21,570
If I just spent more time with her.

435
00:35:22,990 --> 00:35:23,990
Walked her to school.

436
00:35:24,970 --> 00:35:27,530
And gave her what I know she wanted out of our relationship.

437
00:35:28,490 --> 00:35:30,090
So you wanted to give her fake love?

438
00:35:31,470 --> 00:35:32,830
To make her not kill herself?

439
00:35:33,930 --> 00:35:35,730
That sounds like a bad idea, dude.

440
00:35:36,990 --> 00:35:38,290
Then I could have prevented this.

441
00:35:38,890 --> 00:35:39,450
No.

442
00:35:40,610 --> 00:35:42,150
I know I could have prevented this.

443
00:35:43,390 --> 00:35:44,910
Screw the literature club.

444
00:35:45,630 --> 00:35:46,510
Fuck yeah.

445
00:35:47,510 --> 00:35:48,730
Screw the festival.

446
00:35:49,470 --> 00:35:51,850
I just lost my best friend.

447
00:35:53,010 --> 00:35:54,390
Someone I grew up with.

448
00:35:55,190 --> 00:35:56,610
She's gone forever now.

449
00:35:56,610 --> 00:35:58,110
What is this creepy ass music?

450
00:35:59,410 --> 00:36:00,990
Nothing I do can bring her back.

451
00:36:02,770 --> 00:36:05,690
This isn't some game where I can reset and try something different.

452
00:36:09,220 --> 00:36:09,980
Is it not?

453
00:36:11,520 --> 00:36:12,980
I had only one chance.

454
00:36:13,180 --> 00:36:14,300
And I wasn't careful enough.

455
00:36:15,760 --> 00:36:18,180
And now I'll carry this guilt with me until I die.

456
00:36:19,600 --> 00:36:21,600
Nothing in my life is worth more than hers.

457
00:36:23,220 --> 00:36:25,240
But I still couldn't do what she needed from me.

458
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:27,380
God, are you just gonna keep repeating this?

459
00:36:27,860 --> 00:36:28,860
And now...

460
00:36:28,860 --> 00:36:30,520
I can never take it back.

461
00:36:32,980 --> 00:36:33,540
Never.

462
00:36:34,460 --> 00:36:35,220
Never.

463
00:36:35,900 --> 00:36:36,680
Never.

464
00:36:37,940 --> 00:36:39,060
Never.

465
00:36:41,220 --> 00:36:41,780
Never.

466
00:36:48,390 --> 00:36:49,050
And?

467
00:36:51,150 --> 00:36:52,270
What?

468
00:36:59,290 --> 00:37:00,990
What the fuck?

469
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:05,140
What's... uh...

470
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:06,660
Wait a minute, is that...

471
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:09,000
Is this...

472
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:09,560
Sayori?

473
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,040
Wait, hold on.

474
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:12,960
So, this is Yuri.

475
00:37:15,300 --> 00:37:16,140
Wait, who's who?

476
00:37:19,180 --> 00:37:20,240
This is not Suki.

477
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:25,120
This has to be...

478
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:26,980
Wait a minute, why do they look exactly the same?

479
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:29,920
They have the same pen.

480
00:37:30,180 --> 00:37:31,740
Wait, what the fuck is this?

481
00:37:40,950 --> 00:37:49,790
I see an annoying girl running toward me from the distance, waving her arms in the air like she's totally oblivious to any attention she might draw to herself.

482
00:37:50,690 --> 00:37:51,850
That girl is...

483
00:37:51,850 --> 00:37:55,070
My neighbor and good friend since we were children.

484
00:37:55,970 --> 00:38:02,690
You know, the kind of friend you'd never see yourself making today, but kinda just it of works out because you've known each other so long for.

485
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:10,350
We used to walk to school together on days like this, but starting around high school she would weekend more and more frequently and I would get tired of waiting up.

486
00:38:10,870 --> 00:38:14,910
But if she's gonna chase after me like this, I nearly feel better off running away.

487
00:38:15,550 --> 00:38:19,050
However, I just sigh an idol in front of the crosswalk and it's up to me.

488
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:25,640
Yeah, okay.

489
00:38:27,860 --> 00:38:30,160
It's an ordinary school day, like any other.

490
00:38:30,940 --> 00:38:36,200
Mornings are usually the worst, being surrounded by friends and couples, groups walking to school together.

491
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:38,760
Meanwhile, I've always walked to school alone.

492
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:42,700
I always tell myself it's about time I meet some girls or something like that.

493
00:38:42,700 --> 00:38:45,440
But I have no motivation to join any clubs.

494
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:51,420
I'm perfectly content just getting by on the average, while spending my free time anime on games.

495
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:55,620
There's always the anime club, but it's not like there would be any girls in it anyway.

496
00:38:58,880 --> 00:39:02,780
The school day is as ordinary as ever, and it's over before I know it.

497
00:39:03,360 --> 00:39:08,460
After I pack up my things, I stare blankly at the wall, looking for an ounce of motivation.

498
00:39:09,700 --> 00:39:10,180
Clubs!

499
00:39:11,340 --> 00:39:13,240
There really aren't any that interest me.

500
00:39:14,060 --> 00:39:17,660
Besides, most of them would probably be way too demanding for me to want to deal with.

501
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:20,680
I guess I have no choice but to start with the anime club.

502
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:22,320
Oliver?

503
00:39:25,140 --> 00:39:25,560
Monica?

504
00:39:27,160 --> 00:39:29,900
Oh my goodness, I totally didn't expect to see you here!

505
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:31,860
It's been a while, right?

506
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:33,700
Uh, yeah!

507
00:39:34,420 --> 00:39:35,180
It has!

508
00:39:36,340 --> 00:39:37,760
Monica smiles sweetly.

509
00:39:38,220 --> 00:39:39,780
We do know each other well.

510
00:39:40,200 --> 00:39:42,820
We rarely talk, but we were in the same class last year.

511
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:46,100
Monica was probably the most popular girl in class.

512
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:47,840
Smart, beautiful, athletic.

513
00:39:48,660 --> 00:39:50,340
Basically completely out of my league.

514
00:39:50,460 --> 00:39:51,520
Wait a minute, have I read this before?

515
00:39:52,260 --> 00:39:55,580
So having her smile on me so genuinely feels a little...

516
00:39:55,580 --> 00:39:57,440
What did you come in here for anyway?

517
00:39:58,460 --> 00:40:01,740
Oh, I've just been looking for some supplies to use for my club!

518
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:05,180
Do you know if there's any construction paper in here?

519
00:40:06,680 --> 00:40:07,480
Or... markers?

520
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:10,340
I guess you can check the closet.

521
00:40:11,520 --> 00:40:13,040
You're the debate club, right?

522
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:15,220
Haha, about that.

523
00:40:16,420 --> 00:40:17,200
I actually quit it.

524
00:40:18,140 --> 00:40:19,180
Really, you quit?

525
00:40:19,900 --> 00:40:20,340
Yeah.

526
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:24,440
To be honest, I can't stand all the politics around the major clubs.

527
00:40:25,040 --> 00:40:29,100
It feels like nothing but arguing about the budget and publicity and how to prepare for the events.

528
00:40:29,820 --> 00:40:33,320
I'd much rather take something I personally enjoy and make something special out of it.

529
00:40:34,100 --> 00:40:36,440
In that case, what club did you decide to join?

530
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:38,840
Actually, I'm starting a new one.

531
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:40,580
A literature club!

532
00:40:41,340 --> 00:40:42,400
Fucking hell, that scared me.

533
00:40:43,660 --> 00:40:44,060
Literature!

534
00:40:44,860 --> 00:40:46,220
That sounds kinda dull!

535
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,840
How many members do you have so far?

536
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:50,840
Um...

537
00:40:51,900 --> 00:40:53,860
It's kind of embarrassing, but...

538
00:40:53,860 --> 00:40:55,220
There are only three of us so far?

539
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:57,440
It's really hard to find new...

540
00:40:57,440 --> 00:40:57,740
Wait, three!

541
00:41:00,420 --> 00:41:00,820
Alright!

542
00:41:01,360 --> 00:41:03,940
It's really hard to find new members or something that sounds so boring!

543
00:41:04,860 --> 00:41:06,220
Well, I can see that!

544
00:41:06,900 --> 00:41:08,540
But it's really not boring at all, you know?

545
00:41:09,340 --> 00:41:10,380
Literature can be anything!

546
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:12,500
Reading, writing, poetry...

547
00:41:13,040 --> 00:41:16,380
I mean, one of my members even keeps her manga collection in the club room!

548
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:18,680
Wait, really?!

549
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:20,280
Yeah, it's funny, right?

550
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:22,980
She always insists that manga is literature too!

551
00:41:23,540 --> 00:41:25,200
I mean, she's not wrong, I guess.

552
00:41:25,980 --> 00:41:27,500
And besides, a member's a member, right?

553
00:41:28,380 --> 00:41:29,740
Did Monica say she?

554
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:33,560
Hey, Oliver!

555
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:37,340
By any chance, are you still looking for a club to join?

556
00:41:38,560 --> 00:41:39,000
Ah!

557
00:41:40,140 --> 00:41:42,340
I mean, I guess so, but...

558
00:41:42,340 --> 00:41:43,360
In that case...

559
00:41:44,020 --> 00:41:46,000
Is there any chance you would do me a big favor?

560
00:41:46,580 --> 00:41:48,540
I won't ask you to join, but...

561
00:41:48,540 --> 00:41:53,680
If you could get, at the very least, or visit my club, it would make me really happy!

562
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:55,160
Please?

563
00:41:58,060 --> 00:41:58,500
Um...

564
00:41:58,500 --> 00:42:00,700
Well, I guess I have no reason to refuse!

565
00:42:01,600 --> 00:42:03,760
Besides, how could I ever refuse someone like Monica?

566
00:42:04,680 --> 00:42:06,320
Sure, I guess I could check it out!

567
00:42:07,500 --> 00:42:07,940
Ah!

568
00:42:07,940 --> 00:42:08,380
Awesome!

569
00:42:08,380 --> 00:42:10,620
You're really sweet, Oliver, you know that?

570
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:12,280
It's nothing!

571
00:42:12,620 --> 00:42:12,800
Really?

572
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:14,820
Shall we go then?

573
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:17,340
I'll look for the materials another time!

574
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,680
You're more important!

575
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:20,820
Oh, thank you!

576
00:42:21,980 --> 00:42:26,880
And thus, today marks the day I sold my soul to Monica, and her irresistible smile.

577
00:42:27,200 --> 00:42:29,040
Wait, was it Monica last time too?

578
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:33,240
I dejectedly follow Monica across the school and upstairs.

579
00:42:33,680 --> 00:42:36,160
A section of the school I rarely visit.

580
00:42:37,240 --> 00:42:40,400
Monica, full of energy, swings open the classroom door.

581
00:42:44,240 --> 00:42:46,040
And I brought a guest with me!

582
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:47,360
Oh!

583
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:50,320
A... guest?

584
00:42:51,380 --> 00:42:51,940
Seriously?

585
00:42:52,220 --> 00:42:53,920
You brought a boy?!

586
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:55,580
Way to kill the atmosphere!

587
00:42:56,660 --> 00:42:57,920
Don't be mean, Natsuki!

588
00:42:58,520 --> 00:43:00,380
But anyway, welcome to the club, Oliver!

589
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:02,860
Ah...

590
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:06,060
All words escape me in this situation.

591
00:43:06,820 --> 00:43:07,940
This club...

592
00:43:08,620 --> 00:43:10,520
is full of incredibly cute girls!

593
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:12,850
So let me guess...

594
00:43:13,260 --> 00:43:14,720
You're Monica's boyfriend, right?

595
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:16,780
What?!

596
00:43:16,780 --> 00:43:17,540
No!

597
00:43:17,920 --> 00:43:18,900
I'm not!

598
00:43:20,860 --> 00:43:21,680
Natsuki...

599
00:43:21,680 --> 00:43:26,340
The girl with the sour attitude, whose name is apparently Natsuki, is one I don't recognize.

600
00:43:27,060 --> 00:43:29,580
Her small figure makes her look like a first year student.

601
00:43:30,760 --> 00:43:33,420
Anyway, this is Natsuki, energetic as usual.

602
00:43:33,900 --> 00:43:35,740
And this is Yuri, the Vice President.

603
00:43:36,860 --> 00:43:38,280
I... it's nice to meet you.

604
00:43:39,300 --> 00:43:44,960
Yuri, who appears comparably more mature and timid, seems to have a hard time keeping up with someone like Natsuki.

605
00:43:46,720 --> 00:43:47,080
Yeah...

606
00:43:47,080 --> 00:43:48,700
It's nice to meet both of you.

607
00:43:49,920 --> 00:43:53,360
So I ran into Oliver in a classroom, and he decided to come check out the club!

608
00:43:54,200 --> 00:43:55,140
Isn't that great?

609
00:43:56,260 --> 00:43:56,620
Wait!

610
00:43:57,100 --> 00:43:57,460
Monica!

611
00:43:58,460 --> 00:44:01,200
Didn't I tell you to let me know in advance before you brought anyone new?

612
00:44:01,940 --> 00:44:03,620
I was gonna... well...

613
00:44:03,620 --> 00:44:05,080
You know...

614
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:06,160
Sorry, sorry.

615
00:44:06,760 --> 00:44:09,040
I didn't forget that, but I just happened to run into him.

616
00:44:09,860 --> 00:44:12,100
In that case, I should at least make some tea, right?

617
00:44:13,080 --> 00:44:14,200
Yeah, that would be great!

618
00:44:14,860 --> 00:44:16,200
Why don't you come sit down, Oliver?

619
00:44:17,700 --> 00:44:20,320
The girls have a few desks arranged to form a table.

620
00:44:20,700 --> 00:44:22,460
Bro, what is happening in this game right now?

621
00:44:22,980 --> 00:44:25,600
Yuri walks to the corner of the room and opens the closet.

622
00:44:26,660 --> 00:44:29,120
Meanwhile, Monica and Natsuki sit across from each other.

623
00:44:30,080 --> 00:44:32,500
Still feeling awkward, I take a seat next to Monica.

624
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:35,980
So, I know you didn't really plan on coming here.

625
00:44:36,580 --> 00:44:38,460
But we'll make sure you feel right at home, okay?

626
00:44:39,540 --> 00:44:44,400
As president of the Literature Club, it is my duty to make the club fun and exciting for everyone.

627
00:44:45,300 --> 00:44:47,860
I'm surprised there aren't more people in the club yet!

628
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:50,200
It must be hard to start a new club!

629
00:44:51,380 --> 00:44:52,440
You could put it that way.

630
00:44:53,240 --> 00:44:57,200
Not many people are very interested in putting out all the effort to start something brand new.

631
00:44:58,100 --> 00:45:01,260
Especially when it's something that doesn't grab your attention, like literature.

632
00:45:02,500 --> 00:45:05,040
You have to work hard to convince people that you're both fun and worthwhile.

633
00:45:06,060 --> 00:45:09,180
But you make school events like the festival that much more important.

634
00:45:09,800 --> 00:45:13,280
I'm confident that we can all really grow this club together before we graduate.

635
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:14,880
Right, Natsuki?

636
00:45:16,120 --> 00:45:16,640
Well...

637
00:45:16,640 --> 00:45:17,740
I guess.

638
00:45:19,100 --> 00:45:20,580
Natsuki reluctantly agrees.

639
00:45:21,460 --> 00:45:24,000
Such different girls, all interested in the same goal.

640
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:27,720
Monica must have worked really hard just to find these two.

641
00:45:28,080 --> 00:45:31,980
Dude, I still can't get over the fact that they showed that girl hanged from the ceiling.

642
00:45:32,560 --> 00:45:33,720
Like, what the fuck?

643
00:45:35,400 --> 00:45:36,520
That's messed up, bro.

644
00:45:38,880 --> 00:45:41,240
Yuri returns to the table, carrying a tea set.

645
00:45:42,100 --> 00:45:46,320
She carefully places a tea cup in front of each of us before setting down the teapot in the middle.

646
00:45:48,220 --> 00:45:51,620
You keep a whole te- YOU KEEP A WHOLE TEA SET IN THIS CLASSROOM!

647
00:45:52,880 --> 00:45:53,520
Don't worry.

648
00:45:53,860 --> 00:45:55,080
The teachers gave us permission.

649
00:45:56,440 --> 00:45:59,500
After all, doesn't a hot cup of tea help you enjoy a good book?

650
00:46:00,700 --> 00:46:02,500
Uh, I guess?

651
00:46:03,700 --> 00:46:05,700
Haha, don't let yourself get intimidated.

652
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:07,140
Yuri's just trying to impress you.

653
00:46:08,100 --> 00:46:10,000
Huh, that's not...

654
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:11,860
Insulted, Yuri looks away.

655
00:46:13,200 --> 00:46:14,500
I meant that, you know.

656
00:46:15,660 --> 00:46:16,620
I believe you.

657
00:46:17,700 --> 00:46:22,060
Well, tea and reading might not be a pastime for me, but I at least enjoy tea.

658
00:46:22,860 --> 00:46:23,660
I'm glad.

659
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:26,960
Yuri faintly smiles to herself in relief.

660
00:46:27,880 --> 00:46:30,920
So, Oliver, what kinds of things do you like to read?

661
00:46:33,460 --> 00:46:34,340
Well, uh...

662
00:46:34,340 --> 00:46:38,880
Considering how little I've read these past few years, I don't really have a good way of answering that.

663
00:46:40,400 --> 00:46:40,840
MANGA!

664
00:46:41,700 --> 00:46:44,100
I mutter quietly to myself, half-joking.

665
00:46:45,540 --> 00:46:47,000
Natsuki's head suddenly perks up.

666
00:46:47,700 --> 00:46:50,460
It looks like she wants to say something, but she keeps quiet.

667
00:46:51,680 --> 00:46:53,560
N-not much of a reader, I guess.

668
00:46:54,440 --> 00:46:56,180
Well, that can change.

669
00:46:56,740 --> 00:46:57,940
What am I saying?

670
00:46:58,580 --> 00:47:01,300
I spoke without thinking after seeing Yuri's sad smile.

671
00:47:03,400 --> 00:47:04,000
Also...

672
00:47:04,560 --> 00:47:05,480
Sayori isn't here.

673
00:47:07,680 --> 00:47:09,520
Anyway, what about you, Yuri?

674
00:47:10,500 --> 00:47:11,760
Well, let's see.

675
00:47:12,780 --> 00:47:15,420
Yuri traces the rim of her teacup with her finger.

676
00:47:16,240 --> 00:47:20,860
My favorites are usually novels that build deep and complex fantasy worlds.

677
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:25,180
The level of creativity and craftsmanship behind them is amazing to me.

678
00:47:25,980 --> 00:47:29,380
And telling a good story in such a foreign world is equally impressive.

679
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:32,840
Yuri goes on, clearly passionate about her reading.

680
00:47:33,500 --> 00:47:36,460
She seemed so reserved and timid since the moment I walked in.

681
00:47:36,740 --> 00:47:41,580
But it's obvious by the way her eyes light up that she finds her comfort in the world of books, not people.

682
00:47:42,900 --> 00:47:45,000
But you know, I like a lot of things.

683
00:47:46,060 --> 00:47:49,340
Stories with deep psychological elements usually immerse me as well.

684
00:47:50,360 --> 00:47:55,520
Isn't it amazing how a writer can so deliberately take advantage of your own lack of imagination to completely throw you for a loop?

685
00:47:56,440 --> 00:47:58,660
Anyway, I've been reading a lot of horror lately.

686
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:00,040
Ah!

687
00:48:00,220 --> 00:48:01,580
I read a horror book once!

688
00:48:03,240 --> 00:48:06,620
I desperately grasp something I can relate to at the minimal level.

689
00:48:07,580 --> 00:48:10,860
At this rate, Yuri might as well be having a conversation with a rock.

690
00:48:12,120 --> 00:48:12,520
Ahaha!

691
00:48:12,520 --> 00:48:13,960
I'd expect that from you, Yuri.

692
00:48:14,520 --> 00:48:15,880
It suits your personality.

693
00:48:16,980 --> 00:48:17,980
Oh, is that so?

694
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:23,640
Really, if a story makes me think, or takes me to another world, then I really can't put it down.

695
00:48:24,680 --> 00:48:28,060
Surreal horror is often very successful at changing the way you look at the world.

696
00:48:28,660 --> 00:48:29,840
If only for a brief moment.

697
00:48:30,780 --> 00:48:31,200
Ugh!

698
00:48:31,420 --> 00:48:32,300
I hate horror!

699
00:48:33,200 --> 00:48:34,800
Oh, why's that...

700
00:48:34,800 --> 00:48:35,860
Well, I just...

701
00:48:36,840 --> 00:48:39,240
Natsuki's eyes dart over to me for a split second.

702
00:48:40,200 --> 00:48:40,760
Never mind.

703
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:45,200
That's right, you usually like to write about cute things, don't you, Natsuki?

704
00:48:46,080 --> 00:48:46,560
B-what?

705
00:48:47,200 --> 00:48:48,380
Who gives you that idea?

706
00:48:49,320 --> 00:48:51,940
You left a piece of scrap paper behind last club meeting.

707
00:48:52,540 --> 00:48:54,660
It looked like you were working on a poem called...

708
00:48:55,420 --> 00:48:56,440
Don't say it out loud!

709
00:48:57,380 --> 00:48:58,340
And give that back!

710
00:48:59,040 --> 00:48:59,980
Fine, fine.

711
00:49:01,400 --> 00:49:02,080
Natsuki!

712
00:49:02,380 --> 00:49:03,660
You write your own poems?!

713
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:06,980
Uh, well, I guess sometimes?

714
00:49:07,620 --> 00:49:08,720
Why do you care?

715
00:49:09,400 --> 00:49:10,860
I think that's impressive!

716
00:49:11,660 --> 00:49:13,520
Why don't you share them sometime?

717
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:15,220
N-no!

718
00:49:16,580 --> 00:49:18,180
Natsuki averts her eyes.

719
00:49:18,940 --> 00:49:20,340
You wouldn't...

720
00:49:20,340 --> 00:49:21,100
Like them!

721
00:49:22,200 --> 00:49:22,680
Ah!

722
00:49:23,060 --> 00:49:25,440
Not a very confident writer yet?!

723
00:49:26,180 --> 00:49:28,040
I understand how Natsuki feels.

724
00:49:28,740 --> 00:49:31,500
Sharing that level of writing takes more than just confidence.

725
00:49:32,300 --> 00:49:35,120
The truest form of writing is writing to oneself.

726
00:49:36,260 --> 00:49:43,000
You must be willing to open up to your readers, exposing your vulnerabilities, and showing even the deepest reaches of your heart.

727
00:49:44,140 --> 00:49:46,180
Do you have writing experience too, Yuri?

728
00:49:47,560 --> 00:49:52,620
Maybe if you share some of your work, you can set an example, and help Natsuki feel comfortable enough to share hers!

729
00:49:55,320 --> 00:49:57,200
I guess it's the same for Yuri!

730
00:49:58,220 --> 00:50:00,180
We all sit in silence for a moment.

731
00:50:00,620 --> 00:50:01,580
No, we're standing.

732
00:50:02,940 --> 00:50:04,360
Hey, I just got an idea!

733
00:50:05,120 --> 00:50:06,180
How about this?

734
00:50:08,500 --> 00:50:10,780
Natsuki and Yuri look quizzically at Monika.

735
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:14,160
Let's all go home and write a poem of our own!

736
00:50:14,280 --> 00:50:16,780
Oh god, please don't make me go through all that again.

737
00:50:17,340 --> 00:50:18,400
I swear to god.

738
00:50:19,080 --> 00:50:22,040
Then next time we meet, we'll all share them with each other!

739
00:50:23,200 --> 00:50:24,680
That way everyone is even.

740
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:27,040
Um...

741
00:50:28,380 --> 00:50:28,820
Ah!

742
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:31,060
I mean, I thought it was a good idea.

743
00:50:32,480 --> 00:50:32,920
Well...

744
00:50:33,460 --> 00:50:34,800
I think you're right, Monika.

745
00:50:35,500 --> 00:50:39,140
We should probably start finding activities for all of us to participate in together.

746
00:50:40,080 --> 00:50:43,560
I did decide to take on the responsibility of Vice President after all.

747
00:50:44,480 --> 00:50:47,280
I need to do my best to nurture the club as well as its members.

748
00:50:48,460 --> 00:50:52,620
Besides, now that we have a new member, it seems like a good step for us to take.

749
00:50:53,520 --> 00:50:55,060
Do you agree as well, Oliver?

750
00:50:55,760 --> 00:50:56,440
Hold on!

751
00:50:56,920 --> 00:50:58,260
There's still one problem!

752
00:50:59,120 --> 00:50:59,560
Eh?

753
00:50:59,660 --> 00:51:00,100
What's that?

754
00:51:00,820 --> 00:51:06,440
Now that we've reached the most important topic, I bluntly come forth with what's been on my mind the entire time.

755
00:51:07,440 --> 00:51:09,400
I never said I would join this club!

756
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:14,220
Monika may have convinced me to stop by, but I never made any decision!

757
00:51:15,100 --> 00:51:17,610
I still have other clubs to look at and, um...

758
00:51:17,610 --> 00:51:19,450
I lose my train of thought.

759
00:51:19,870 --> 00:51:22,750
All three girls stare back at me with dejected eyes.

760
00:51:23,570 --> 00:51:24,570
But, but...

761
00:51:24,570 --> 00:51:25,590
I'm sorry.

762
00:51:25,870 --> 00:51:26,610
I thought...

763
00:51:27,310 --> 00:51:27,590
Huh!

764
00:51:29,530 --> 00:51:32,790
The girls exchange glances before Monika turns back to me.

765
00:51:34,050 --> 00:51:36,170
I... I guess I need to tell you the truth, Oliver.

766
00:51:36,650 --> 00:51:37,990
The thing is...

767
00:51:38,590 --> 00:51:41,290
We don't have enough members yet to form an official club.

768
00:51:42,050 --> 00:51:43,070
We need four.

769
00:51:44,090 --> 00:51:47,130
And I've been trying really, really, really hard to find new members.

770
00:51:47,630 --> 00:51:49,790
And if we don't find one more before the festival...

771
00:51:52,130 --> 00:51:52,570
I...

772
00:51:52,570 --> 00:51:54,530
I'm defenseless against these girls!

773
00:51:55,830 --> 00:51:58,610
How am I supposed to make a clear-headed decision when it's like this?

774
00:51:59,350 --> 00:52:02,250
I would feel terrible for letting everyone down in this situation.

775
00:52:03,230 --> 00:52:05,410
And besides, the club itself seems pretty relaxed.

776
00:52:06,590 --> 00:52:10,790
So if writing poems is the price I need to pay in order to spend every day with these beautiful girls...

777
00:52:12,390 --> 00:52:12,750
Right!

778
00:52:13,670 --> 00:52:15,010
Okay, I've decided then!

779
00:52:16,090 --> 00:52:17,950
I'll join the Literature Club!

780
00:52:19,030 --> 00:52:21,350
One by one, the girls' eyes light up.

781
00:52:22,130 --> 00:52:23,390
Oh my goodness, really?

782
00:52:23,990 --> 00:52:25,430
Do you really mean that, Oliver?

783
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:26,790
Yeah!

784
00:52:27,750 --> 00:52:29,190
It could be fun, right?

785
00:52:30,550 --> 00:52:32,170
You really did scare me for a moment.

786
00:52:32,870 --> 00:52:36,170
I mean, if you really just left after all this, I would be super pissed.

787
00:52:37,830 --> 00:52:39,210
Oliver, I'm so happy!

788
00:52:39,870 --> 00:52:41,750
We can become an official club now!

789
00:52:42,350 --> 00:52:43,730
Thank you so much for this!

790
00:52:43,910 --> 00:52:44,730
You're really amazing!

791
00:52:44,830 --> 00:52:45,630
The best person on earth!

792
00:52:45,730 --> 00:52:47,230
Wow, can we thank you enough?!

793
00:52:47,870 --> 00:52:49,990
I'll do everything I can to give you a great time, okay?

794
00:52:51,050 --> 00:52:52,090
Ah-ha-ha!

795
00:52:52,370 --> 00:52:52,810
Thanks!

796
00:52:53,150 --> 00:52:53,950
I guess?

797
00:52:55,150 --> 00:52:55,950
Okay, everyone!

798
00:52:56,970 --> 00:52:59,710
I think with that, we can officially end today's meeting on a good note!

799
00:53:00,870 --> 00:53:02,370
Everyone remember tonight's assignment!

800
00:53:02,910 --> 00:53:05,510
Write a poem to bring to the next meeting so we can all share!

801
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:08,170
Monica looks over to me once more.

802
00:53:09,090 --> 00:53:11,890
Oliver, I look forward to seeing how you express yourself!

803
00:53:11,890 --> 00:53:13,070
He-he-he!

804
00:53:14,170 --> 00:53:14,610
He-he-he!

805
00:53:15,570 --> 00:53:19,650
Can I really impress the class star Monica with my mediocre writing skills?

806
00:53:20,690 --> 00:53:23,390
I already feel the anxiety welling up inside me.

807
00:53:24,830 --> 00:53:28,250
