But anyway, I'm really into it.

1082
01:04:37,720 --> 01:04:38,840
The book, I mean.

1083
01:04:40,020 --> 01:04:41,700
Not the thing about the limbs.

1084
01:04:43,480 --> 01:04:44,640
That's kind of...

1085
01:04:45,420 --> 01:04:46,780
That's kind of dark, isn't it?

1086
01:04:47,780 --> 01:04:49,740
Yuri made it sound like it was going to be a nice story.

1087
01:04:50,060 --> 01:04:51,900
So that dark turn came from nowhere.

1088
01:04:53,980 --> 01:04:54,380
Ah...

1089
01:04:54,380 --> 01:04:56,400
Are you not a fan of that sort of thing, Oliver?

1090
01:04:57,380 --> 01:04:58,600
No, it's not that!

1091
01:04:59,280 --> 01:05:02,100
I mean, I can definitely enjoy these kinds of stories!

1092
01:05:02,320 --> 01:05:03,120
So don't worry!

1093
01:05:03,760 --> 01:05:04,800
I hope so.

1094
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:08,540
Yeah, I totally forgot that Yuri is into those things.

1095
01:05:09,380 --> 01:05:11,720
She's so shy and reclusive on the outside.

1096
01:05:12,080 --> 01:05:14,020
But her mind seems to be completely different.

1097
01:05:15,520 --> 01:05:17,840
It's just that this kind of story...

1098
01:05:18,760 --> 01:05:22,400
It's the kind that challenges you to look at life from a strange new perspective.

1099
01:05:23,180 --> 01:05:26,240
When horrible things happen not just because someone wants to be evil...

1100
01:05:27,180 --> 01:05:32,580
But because the world is full of horrible people and we're all worthless anyway...

1101
01:05:32,580 --> 01:05:34,100
Then suddenly...

1102
01:05:34,100 --> 01:05:35,500
I'm rambling, aren't I?

1103
01:05:36,260 --> 01:05:36,920
Not again.

1104
01:05:37,480 --> 01:05:38,480
I'm sorry.

1105
01:05:39,420 --> 01:05:39,860
Hey!

1106
01:05:40,440 --> 01:05:41,320
Don't apologize!

1107
01:05:42,300 --> 01:05:44,220
I haven't lost interest or anything!

1108
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:46,340
Well...

1109
01:05:46,340 --> 01:05:47,660
I guess it's alright.

1110
01:05:51,100 --> 01:05:53,720
But I feel like I should let you know that I have this problem.

1111
01:05:54,920 --> 01:05:57,780
When I let things like books and writing fill my thoughts...

1112
01:06:00,560 --> 01:06:01,000
What?!

1113
01:06:01,000 --> 01:06:03,460
I kind of forget to pay attention to other people.

1114
01:06:05,280 --> 01:06:07,520
So I'm sorry if I end up saying something strange.

1115
01:06:08,160 --> 01:06:09,880
And please stop me if I'm...

1116
01:06:09,880 --> 01:06:10,760
Talking too much.

1117
01:06:11,920 --> 01:06:12,440
That's...

1118
01:06:12,440 --> 01:06:14,620
I really don't think you need to worry!

1119
01:06:15,600 --> 01:06:17,700
That just means you're a passionate...

1120
01:06:17,700 --> 01:06:17,920
Being!

1121
01:06:19,260 --> 01:06:20,780
The least I can do is listen!

1122
01:06:21,480 --> 01:06:23,240
It's a literature club after all!

1123
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:25,520
Uh...

1124
01:06:26,220 --> 01:06:26,740
That's...

1125
01:06:27,360 --> 01:06:28,060
Well that's true.

1126
01:06:29,240 --> 01:06:29,980
In fact!

1127
01:06:30,740 --> 01:06:33,540
I might as well get started reading it, right?!

1128
01:06:34,180 --> 01:06:34,700
Yes!

1129
01:06:34,700 --> 01:06:34,820
Yes!

1130
01:06:35,360 --> 01:06:37,940
I mean, you don't have to, but...

1131
01:06:37,940 --> 01:06:38,280
Haha!

1132
01:06:38,560 --> 01:06:40,100
What are you saying?!

1133
01:06:41,760 --> 01:06:42,740
Let me just get the book!

1134
01:06:44,080 --> 01:06:46,580
I quickly retrieve the book that I had put into my bag.

1135
01:06:48,320 --> 01:06:48,680
Alright!

1136
01:06:49,420 --> 01:06:50,720
It's fine if I sit here, right?!

1137
01:06:51,920 --> 01:06:53,860
I slip into the seat next to Yuri's.

1138
01:06:54,720 --> 01:06:54,920
Ah!

1139
01:06:56,740 --> 01:06:57,100
Yeah...

1140
01:06:57,100 --> 01:06:57,700
Are you sure?!

1141
01:06:58,840 --> 01:06:59,800
You seem a little apprehensive!

1142
01:07:01,860 --> 01:07:02,460
That's...

1143
01:07:02,460 --> 01:07:03,540
I'm sorry.

1144
01:07:04,340 --> 01:07:06,020
It's not that I don't want you to.

1145
01:07:06,680 --> 01:07:08,820
It's just something I'm not very used to.

1146
01:07:09,600 --> 01:07:10,800
That is...

1147
01:07:10,800 --> 01:07:14,060
Reading in company with someone who said this is so stupid.

1148
01:07:14,680 --> 01:07:15,560
I see!

1149
01:07:16,760 --> 01:07:18,100
Watch your dance!

1150
01:07:18,100 --> 01:07:19,500
Ah!

1151
01:07:21,280 --> 01:07:22,260
Ha ha ha ha ha!

1152
01:07:22,940 --> 01:07:26,160
Ha ha ha ha ha!

1153
01:07:32,410 --> 01:07:34,130
Ha ha ha ha ha!

1154
01:07:46,670 --> 01:07:47,150
Yes!

1155
01:07:49,230 --> 01:07:49,950
Well...

1156
01:07:53,110 --> 01:07:55,930
He he he he...

1157
01:07:57,770 --> 01:07:58,490
Okay...

1158
01:07:59,890 --> 01:08:00,610
Well...

1159
01:08:00,610 --> 01:08:01,550
I

1160
01:08:05,990 --> 01:08:07,750
can't do this stupid voice!

1161
01:08:14,390 --> 01:08:18,010
Ah, I need to calm down.

1162
01:08:21,750 --> 01:08:23,090
Okay, wait, wait.

1163
01:08:23,470 --> 01:08:24,550
Wait, hold on, give me a sec.

1164
01:08:31,440 --> 01:08:33,020
Okay, focus.

1165
01:08:33,840 --> 01:08:34,780
Focus, dammit.

1166
01:08:35,560 --> 01:08:36,740
Oh my god, I'm crying.

1167
01:08:41,320 --> 01:08:43,020
Wait, wait, what happened for this?

1168
01:08:44,860 --> 01:08:48,400
Uh... Which one is the latest?

1169
01:08:48,600 --> 01:08:49,560
I don't fucking understand.

1170
01:08:50,360 --> 01:08:51,120
Alright.

1171
01:08:57,140 --> 01:08:59,180
I can't fucking do it.

1172
01:09:04,220 --> 01:09:05,480
Oh my god.

1173
01:09:09,420 --> 01:09:10,520
Okay, focus.

1174
01:09:10,860 --> 01:09:11,420
Log in.

1175
01:09:12,540 --> 01:09:13,980
This is so stupid.

1176
01:09:19,290 --> 01:09:22,250
Well, just tell me if I've not distracted you or anything!

1177
01:09:23,210 --> 01:09:23,810
Alright.

1178
01:09:24,730 --> 01:09:26,930
I open the book and start the prologue.

1179
01:09:27,410 --> 01:09:30,210
I soon understand what Yuri means about reading and company.

1180
01:09:31,110 --> 01:09:33,910
It's as if I can feel a presence over my shoulder as I read.

1181
01:09:34,630 --> 01:09:36,410
It's not a particularly bad thing.

1182
01:09:37,010 --> 01:09:39,730
Maybe a little distracting, but the feeling is somewhat comforting.

1183
01:09:40,630 --> 01:09:42,190
Yuri is in the corner of my eye.

1184
01:09:42,770 --> 01:09:45,690
I realize that she's not actually looking at her own book.

1185
01:09:46,170 --> 01:09:47,310
I glance over.

1186
01:09:47,910 --> 01:09:50,250
It looks like she's reading from my book instead.

1187
01:09:51,310 --> 01:09:51,870
Sorry.

1188
01:09:52,590 --> 01:09:54,050
I was just bathing in the feeling.

1189
01:09:54,810 --> 01:09:57,450
Yuri, you really apologize a lot, don't you?

1190
01:09:58,290 --> 01:09:59,570
I... I do?

1191
01:10:00,270 --> 01:10:01,610
I don't really mean to.

1192
01:10:02,290 --> 01:10:02,850
Sorry.

1193
01:10:03,790 --> 01:10:04,950
I mean...

1194
01:10:06,590 --> 01:10:07,230
Here!

1195
01:10:07,490 --> 01:10:08,550
This should work, right?

1196
01:10:09,630 --> 01:10:12,790
I slide my desk until it's up against Yuri's.

1197
01:10:13,150 --> 01:10:15,210
And hold my book more between the two of them.

1198
01:10:16,430 --> 01:10:17,070
Ah...

1199
01:10:17,070 --> 01:10:18,670
I suppose so.

1200
01:10:24,410 --> 01:10:26,670
Yuri timidly closes her own copy.

1201
01:10:28,170 --> 01:10:31,510
Once we each lead in a little bit, our shoulders are almost touching.

1202
01:10:32,450 --> 01:10:36,810
It feels like my left arm is in the way, so instead I use my right hand to hold the book open.

1203
01:10:38,090 --> 01:10:38,490
Ah!

1204
01:10:38,890 --> 01:10:41,490
I guess that makes it kind of difficult to turn the page!

1205
01:10:42,270 --> 01:10:42,670
Here.

1206
01:10:43,970 --> 01:10:44,710
Oh, here we go.

1207
01:10:45,910 --> 01:10:49,550
Yuri takes her left arm and holds the left side of the book between her thumb and forefinger.

1208
01:10:50,770 --> 01:10:51,170
Ah!

1209
01:10:52,690 --> 01:10:56,530
I do the same with my right arm on the right side of the book.

1210
01:10:57,150 --> 01:11:01,370
That way I turn a page and Yuri slides it under her thumb after it flips to her side.

1211
01:11:02,150 --> 01:11:06,410
But in holding it like this, we're huddled even closer together than before.

1212
01:11:07,230 --> 01:11:08,970
It's actually kind of distracting me.

1213
01:11:09,590 --> 01:11:14,190
It's as if I can feel the warmth of Yuri's face, and she's in the corner of my vision.

1214
01:11:15,450 --> 01:11:16,330
Are you ready?

1215
01:11:17,650 --> 01:11:18,130
Huh?!

1216
01:11:18,950 --> 01:11:20,170
To turn the page...

1217
01:11:21,210 --> 01:11:21,610
Ha!

1218
01:11:21,610 --> 01:11:22,010
Sorry!

1219
01:11:22,970 --> 01:11:25,170
I think I got a bit distracted for a second!

1220
01:11:25,930 --> 01:11:28,890
I glance over at Yuri's face again, and our eyes meet.

1221
01:11:29,610 --> 01:11:31,650
I don't know how I'll be able to keep up with her.

1222
01:11:33,130 --> 01:11:33,530
Ah...

1223
01:11:33,530 --> 01:11:34,370
That's okay.

1224
01:11:35,430 --> 01:11:37,110
You're not as used to reading, right?

1225
01:11:38,330 --> 01:11:40,690
I don't mind being patient if it takes you a bit longer.

1226
01:11:41,710 --> 01:11:43,230
That's probably the least I can do.

1227
01:11:44,430 --> 01:11:46,010
Since you've been so patient with me.

1228
01:11:46,990 --> 01:11:47,390
Yeah!

1229
01:11:48,590 --> 01:11:48,990
Thanks!

1230
01:11:49,750 --> 01:11:50,970
We continue reading.

1231
01:11:51,550 --> 01:11:54,350
Yuri no longer asks me if I'm ready to turn the page.

1232
01:11:54,910 --> 01:11:57,670
Instead, I just assume that she finishes the page before me.

1233
01:11:57,870 --> 01:11:59,730
So I turn it by my own volition.

1234
01:12:00,930 --> 01:12:03,310
What if she never ends up finishing the page?!

1235
01:12:03,310 --> 01:12:04,510
Then I'm just being an asshole!

1236
01:12:05,270 --> 01:12:07,550
We continue the first chapter in silence.

1237
01:12:08,290 --> 01:12:11,590
Even so, turning each page almost feels like an intimate exchange.

1238
01:12:12,030 --> 01:12:12,850
Oh my god.

1239
01:12:13,570 --> 01:12:19,310
My thumb gently letting go of the page, letting it flutter over to her side as she catches it under her own thumb.

1240
01:12:20,310 --> 01:12:21,030
Hey Yuri!

1241
01:12:21,750 --> 01:12:23,890
This might be a silly thought, but...

1242
01:12:23,890 --> 01:12:26,590
The main character kind of reminds me of you a little bit!

1243
01:12:27,530 --> 01:12:28,010
Eh?

1244
01:12:28,990 --> 01:12:31,090
No, I don't relate to this character at all.

1245
01:12:32,190 --> 01:12:33,050
Definitely not.

1246
01:12:33,990 --> 01:12:34,470
Really?

1247
01:12:35,530 --> 01:12:38,910
I was just thinking the way she second guesses things she says and all that!

1248
01:12:40,470 --> 01:12:40,570
Ah.

1249
01:12:41,490 --> 01:12:42,850
That's what you were talking about.

1250
01:12:43,610 --> 01:12:44,130
Sorry.

1251
01:12:44,750 --> 01:12:47,430
I thought you meant... something else about her.

1252
01:12:48,850 --> 01:12:49,890
Something else?!

1253
01:12:49,890 --> 01:12:51,110
Never mind.

1254
01:12:51,590 --> 01:12:53,230
We didn't even get that far yet.

1255
01:12:53,770 --> 01:12:55,970
So I don't know why that came into my head.

1256
01:12:58,170 --> 01:12:58,770
Yuri!

1257
01:12:59,250 --> 01:13:00,890
Are you feeling alright?!

1258
01:13:01,750 --> 01:13:02,070
Huh?

1259
01:13:03,110 --> 01:13:05,590
Yuri's been a little fidgety ever since we started reading.

1260
01:13:10,200 --> 01:13:11,700
Oh my god.

1261
01:13:14,220 --> 01:13:15,360
Give me a moment.

1262
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:38,800
Oh my god, this is horrible.

1263
01:13:41,640 --> 01:13:43,140
Come on, wake up man.

1264
01:13:43,680 --> 01:13:44,500
Fucking...

1265
01:13:44,500 --> 01:13:45,600
Pull yourself together.

1266
01:13:48,280 --> 01:13:49,260
Let's go.

1267
01:13:49,840 --> 01:13:50,600
Enter character.

1268
01:13:52,880 --> 01:13:55,340
You can rest if you're feeling sick or something!

1269
01:13:56,180 --> 01:13:58,060
Your breathing is a little...

1270
01:13:58,060 --> 01:13:58,920
My breathing?

1271
01:13:59,820 --> 01:14:01,480
Yuri puts her hand on her chest.

1272
01:14:01,720 --> 01:14:03,100
As if to feel her heartbeat.

1273
01:14:04,320 --> 01:14:05,100
I... I...

1274
01:14:05,100 --> 01:14:06,240
I didn't even notice.

1275
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:08,420
Anyway, I'm... fine.

1276
01:14:08,980 --> 01:14:10,280
I just need some...

1277
01:14:10,280 --> 01:14:11,340
Water.

1278
01:14:12,320 --> 01:14:12,840
Alright!

1279
01:14:13,200 --> 01:14:14,020
Don't push yourself!

1280
01:14:15,880 --> 01:14:19,060
Yuri stands up and practically rushes out of the classroom.

1281
01:14:19,960 --> 01:14:21,700
What on earth was that about?

1282
01:14:23,040 --> 01:14:23,600
Oliver?

1283
01:14:24,200 --> 01:14:25,620
Did something happen just now?

1284
01:14:26,600 --> 01:14:26,880
Eh?

1285
01:14:27,700 --> 01:14:28,740
I've no idea.

1286
01:14:29,880 --> 01:14:32,100
Yuri was acting a little strange, I guess.

1287
01:14:33,300 --> 01:14:34,120
So you...

1288
01:14:34,840 --> 01:14:35,780
So you don't know anything?

1289
01:14:36,740 --> 01:14:38,220
Sorry, I can't say I do!

1290
01:14:38,920 --> 01:14:40,260
Are you worried about her?

1291
01:14:41,540 --> 01:14:42,100
No...

1292
01:14:43,120 --> 01:14:44,060
Not really.

1293
01:14:44,740 --> 01:14:47,060
I was just making sure that you didn't do anything to her.

1294
01:14:47,720 --> 01:14:48,240
No!

1295
01:14:48,540 --> 01:14:48,840
Nothing!

1296
01:14:50,060 --> 01:14:51,560
Don't worry, I believe you silly.

1297
01:14:52,440 --> 01:14:54,580
Yuri just does this sometimes, so it's nothing alarming.

1298
01:14:55,600 --> 01:14:55,980
Alright!

1299
01:14:56,320 --> 01:14:57,220
If you say so!

1300
01:14:59,460 --> 01:14:59,980
Anyway...

1301
01:14:59,980 --> 01:15:02,420
Why don't we start with sharing our poems with each other?

1302
01:15:03,220 --> 01:15:03,520
Eh?

1303
01:15:04,680 --> 01:15:06,040
Should we wait for Yuri?

1304
01:15:09,860 --> 01:15:11,420
Well, she might be a while.

1305
01:15:12,020 --> 01:15:12,640
So I just...

1306
01:15:12,640 --> 01:15:13,940
Get started without her.

1307
01:15:15,160 --> 01:15:16,000
Is that okay?

1308
01:15:17,000 --> 01:15:17,520
Yeah!

1309
01:15:22,280 --> 01:15:23,760
Oh my god!

1310
01:15:33,330 --> 01:15:34,850
I can't!

1311
01:15:35,170 --> 01:15:36,350
Dude, my cheeks are hurting.

1312
01:15:39,160 --> 01:15:40,140
Think of sad things.

1313
01:15:42,220 --> 01:15:42,700
Okay.

1314
01:15:45,580 --> 01:15:45,980
Yeah!

1315
01:15:46,400 --> 01:15:47,340
I was just asking!

1316
01:15:48,280 --> 01:15:49,100
I stand up.

1317
01:15:49,620 --> 01:15:52,100
I make a mental note of where I left off in the book.

1318
01:15:52,240 --> 01:15:53,800
Then slip it back into my bag.

1319
01:15:56,600 --> 01:15:58,340
Who should I show my poem to first?

1320
01:15:59,900 --> 01:16:01,100
Wait, uh, wait a minute.

1321
01:16:01,900 --> 01:16:02,720
What about Yuri?

1322
01:16:03,300 --> 01:16:04,100
Wait, where's...

1323
01:16:05,140 --> 01:16:07,220
She ran out to get water and now she's not here?

1324
01:16:07,480 --> 01:16:08,120
Or what?

1325
01:16:09,280 --> 01:16:09,640
Natsuki.

1326
01:16:10,740 --> 01:16:13,440
I told Natsuki I was interested in her poems yesterday.

1327
01:16:14,020 --> 01:16:15,020
Wait, what do you mean yesterday?

1328
01:16:16,000 --> 01:16:16,760
Was there a yesterday?

1329
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:20,140
It's probably only fair if I shared mine with her first.

1330
01:16:20,220 --> 01:16:21,580
Oh yeah, right, we wrote a poem.

1331
01:16:21,780 --> 01:16:21,840
True.

1332
01:16:30,600 --> 01:16:31,760
What the fuck?!

1333
01:16:32,820 --> 01:16:35,200
Oliver, if you're not gonna take this club seriously, then go home!

1334
01:16:36,020 --> 01:16:36,760
Th- w-what?!

1335
01:16:39,300 --> 01:16:39,660
Harsh?!

1336
01:16:39,660 --> 01:16:42,660
What, you expect me to believe that you actually put effort into this?

1337
01:16:43,400 --> 01:16:44,480
Do you think I'm stupid?

1338
01:16:45,340 --> 01:16:46,460
I'm not a writer!

1339
01:16:47,660 --> 01:16:50,040
Maybe it's not very good, but yeah, I did put in effort!

1340
01:16:50,720 --> 01:16:52,840
We all start somewhere, right?!

1341
01:16:53,400 --> 01:16:57,540
If you're still proud of the first poem you ever wrote, then I'd like to read it!

1342
01:16:59,800 --> 01:17:00,780
Painful to think about?!

1343
01:17:02,700 --> 01:17:03,140
Fine.

1344
01:17:04,240 --> 01:17:05,120
Well, sorry.

1345
01:17:06,320 --> 01:17:07,360
You'll get better anyway.

1346
01:17:08,480 --> 01:17:10,900
I'd tell you what to improve, but you're better off just trying again.

1347
01:17:11,840 --> 01:17:12,500
Fair enough!

1348
01:17:13,440 --> 01:17:14,800
Well, to each their own, I guess.

1349
01:17:15,860 --> 01:17:17,500
Anyway, I guess I gotta share mine now.

1350
01:17:18,380 --> 01:17:20,020
Knowing you, you'll probably think it's stupid.

1351
01:17:22,360 --> 01:17:30,280
Eagles can fly, monkeys can climb, crickets can leap, horses can race, owls can seek, cheetahs can run, eagles can fly- But that's about it.

1352
01:17:32,040 --> 01:17:32,440
Yeah.

1353
01:17:33,180 --> 01:17:34,720
I told you that you weren't gonna like it.

1354
01:17:35,440 --> 01:17:36,420
I LIKE IT!

1355
01:17:37,360 --> 01:17:37,760
What?

1356
01:17:38,440 --> 01:17:39,440
Just be honest!

1357
01:17:40,120 --> 01:17:40,960
I am!

1358
01:17:41,700 --> 01:17:44,360
Why are you so convinced that I wouldn't like it?!

1359
01:17:45,660 --> 01:17:46,180
Well...

1360
01:17:47,120 --> 01:17:47,640
Because...

1361
01:17:47,640 --> 01:17:50,940
Everyone in high school thinks that writing has to be all sophisticated and stuff.

1362
01:17:51,320 --> 01:17:53,320
So people don't even take my writing seriously!

1363
01:17:54,100 --> 01:17:57,620
But isn't the point of poems for people to express themselves?!

1364
01:17:57,620 --> 01:18:00,400
Your writing style wouldn't make your message any less valid!

1365
01:18:01,460 --> 01:18:02,500
Yes, exactly!

1366
01:18:03,360 --> 01:18:05,880
I like it when it's easy to read, but it hits you hard.

1367
01:18:06,600 --> 01:18:07,520
Like in this poem.

1368
01:18:09,140 --> 01:18:11,800
Seeing everyone around you do great things can be really disheartening.

1369
01:18:12,300 --> 01:18:13,860
So I decided to write about it.

1370
01:18:14,720 --> 01:18:16,080
Yeah, I understand!

1371
01:18:17,060 --> 01:18:21,740
But the other nice thing about simple writing is that it puts more weight on the wordplay.

1372
01:18:22,600 --> 01:18:25,820
Like I set up for a rhyme at the end, but then made it fall flat on purpose.

1373
01:18:26,580 --> 01:18:28,280
It helps bring out the feeling in the last line.

1374
01:18:29,280 --> 01:18:30,080
So you did!

1375
01:18:30,600 --> 01:18:32,660
I guess more went into it than I realized!

1376
01:18:33,760 --> 01:18:35,000
That's what it means to be a pro.

1377
01:18:35,800 --> 01:18:37,020
I'm glad you learned something.

1378
01:18:37,860 --> 01:18:39,920
Didn't expect that from the youngest one here, did you?

1379
01:18:40,700 --> 01:18:41,140
Yeah!

1380
01:18:41,520 --> 01:18:42,440
I guess not!

1381
01:18:43,160 --> 01:18:45,560
I decide to humor her with that last comment.

1382
01:18:46,280 --> 01:18:48,280
I don't really care how old everyone is.

1383
01:18:48,500 --> 01:18:51,480
But if Natsuki is feeling proud, then I won't take that away from her.

1384
01:18:55,480 --> 01:18:57,160
Oh, let me guess...

1385
01:18:57,160 --> 01:18:58,360
Who should I pick next?

1386
01:18:59,160 --> 01:18:59,600
Monica!

1387
01:19:02,000 --> 01:19:02,740
Hi Oliver!

1388
01:19:03,360 --> 01:19:04,760
Having a good time so far?

1389
01:19:05,780 --> 01:19:06,220
Yeah!

1390
01:19:07,280 --> 01:19:07,720
Good!

1391
01:19:08,000 --> 01:19:08,680
Glad to hear it.

1392
01:19:09,480 --> 01:19:11,460
By the way, since you're new on everything...

1393
01:19:12,040 --> 01:19:16,920
If you ever have any suggestions for the club, like new activities or things we can do better...

1394
01:19:16,920 --> 01:19:18,400
I'm always listening.

1395
01:19:19,020 --> 01:19:20,660
Don't be afraid to bring things up, okay?

1396
01:19:21,580 --> 01:19:22,020
Alright!

1397
01:19:22,540 --> 01:19:23,640
I'll keep that in mind!

1398
01:19:24,460 --> 01:19:26,400
Of course I'll be afraid to bring things up.

1399
01:19:27,160 --> 01:19:30,680
I'm much better off just going with the flow until I'm more settled in.

1400
01:19:32,340 --> 01:19:32,760
Anyway...

1401
01:19:32,760 --> 01:19:34,000
Want to share your poem with me?

1402
01:19:34,820 --> 01:19:36,700
It's kind of embarrassing, but...

1403
01:19:36,700 --> 01:19:37,820
I guess I have to!

1404
01:19:39,580 --> 01:19:40,480
Don't worry, Oliver.

1405
01:19:40,960 --> 01:19:42,760
We're all a little embarrassed today, you know.

1406
01:19:43,680 --> 01:19:46,520
But it's that sort of barrier that we'll all learn to get past soon.

1407
01:19:47,260 --> 01:19:47,740
Yeah!

1408
01:19:47,940 --> 01:19:48,360
That's true!

1409
01:19:49,160 --> 01:19:50,560
I hand Monica my poem.

1410
01:19:51,620 --> 01:19:51,900
Mmm!

1411
01:19:52,740 --> 01:19:53,880
Great job, Oliver!

1412
01:19:54,340 --> 01:19:56,420
I almost got an ooh in my head while reading it.

1413
01:19:56,860 --> 01:19:58,200
It's really metaphorical.

1414
01:19:58,620 --> 01:20:01,720
I'm not sure why, but I didn't expect you to go for something so deep.

1415
01:20:02,380 --> 01:20:04,080
I guess I underestimated you.

1416
01:20:04,920 --> 01:20:07,960
It's easiest for me to keep everyone's expectations low.

1417
01:20:08,980 --> 01:20:11,600
That way, it always counts when I put in some effort!

1418
01:20:13,220 --> 01:20:14,180
That's not very fair.

1419
01:20:14,820 --> 01:20:16,220
Well, I guess it worked anyway.

1420
01:20:17,120 --> 01:20:19,080
You know that Yuri likes this kind of writing, right?

1421
01:20:20,260 --> 01:20:22,360
Writing that's full of imagery and symbolism?

1422
01:20:23,420 --> 01:20:26,380
Sometimes I feel like Yuri's mind is just totally detached from reality!

1423
01:20:27,240 --> 01:20:28,940
I don't mean that, like it's a bad thing though.

1424
01:20:29,880 --> 01:20:32,940
But sometimes I get the impression that she's just totally given up on people.

1425
01:20:33,880 --> 01:20:38,080
She spends so much time in her own head, and it's probably a much more interesting place for her.

1426
01:20:39,040 --> 01:20:41,560
But that's why she gets so happy when you treat her with a lot of kindness.

1427
01:20:42,560 --> 01:20:44,460
I don't think she's used to being indulged like that.

1428
01:20:45,240 --> 01:20:47,540
She must be really starved for social interaction.

1429
01:20:47,780 --> 01:20:49,820
So don't blame her for coming on a little strongly.

1430
01:20:50,740 --> 01:20:51,440
Like earlier.

1431
01:20:53,320 --> 01:20:53,880
Wait, what?

1432
01:20:55,220 --> 01:20:55,780
What do you mean?

1433
01:20:58,830 --> 01:21:00,270
Does she know about our reading session?

1434
01:21:00,890 --> 01:21:01,730
What's happening here?

1435
01:21:03,530 --> 01:21:07,290
I think if she gets too stimulated, she ends up withdrawing and looking for alone time.

1436
01:21:07,830 --> 01:21:08,930
Oh, is that what happened?

1437
01:21:10,390 --> 01:21:11,770
Suddenly the door opens.

1438
01:21:14,980 --> 01:21:15,580
I'm back.

1439
01:21:16,200 --> 01:21:17,380
Did I miss anything?

1440
01:21:18,260 --> 01:21:19,040
Not really.

1441
01:21:19,620 --> 01:21:21,800
Well, we all started sharing our poems with each other.

1442
01:21:22,640 --> 01:21:22,980
Yeah?

1443
01:21:23,840 --> 01:21:24,320
Already?

1444
01:21:25,460 --> 01:21:26,800
I'm sorry for being late.

1445
01:21:27,500 --> 01:21:28,600
No need to apologize.

1446
01:21:29,560 --> 01:21:32,860
We still have plenty of time, so I'm more glad that you took all the time you needed.

1447
01:21:33,720 --> 01:21:34,160
Alright.

1448
01:21:34,900 --> 01:21:35,500
Thanks, Monica.

1449
01:21:36,420 --> 01:21:38,500
I suppose I should go get my poem now.

1450
01:21:39,540 --> 01:21:41,120
Anyway, you wanna read my poem now?

1451
01:21:42,020 --> 01:21:43,220
Don't worry, I'm not very good.

1452
01:21:44,080 --> 01:21:47,240
You sound pretty confident for someone who claims to be not very good.

1453
01:21:48,480 --> 01:21:50,400
Well, that's because I have to sound confident.

1454
01:21:51,200 --> 01:21:53,040
That doesn't mean I always feel that way, you know?

1455
01:21:53,660 --> 01:21:54,400
I see!

1456
01:21:55,300 --> 01:21:56,640
Well, let's read it then!

1457
01:21:58,480 --> 01:21:59,500
Hole in wall.

1458
01:22:00,240 --> 01:22:00,780
Wait.

1459
01:22:02,140 --> 01:22:04,100
Is this the, uh...

1460
01:22:04,640 --> 01:22:06,500
The follow-up to bean in mouth?

1461
01:22:07,820 --> 01:22:09,340
But he wasn't looking at me.

1462
01:22:09,720 --> 01:22:12,080
Confused, I frantically glance at my surroundings.

1463
01:22:12,400 --> 01:22:15,000
But my burned eyes can no longer see color.

1464
01:22:15,580 --> 01:22:17,160
Are there others in this room?

1465
01:22:17,280 --> 01:22:17,940
Are they talking?

1466
01:22:17,940 --> 01:22:19,920
Or are they simply poems?

1467
01:22:20,200 --> 01:22:21,640
On flat sheets of paper!

1468
01:22:22,740 --> 01:22:25,760
The sound of frantic scrawling playing tricks on my ears.

1469
01:22:26,240 --> 01:22:27,860
The room begins to crinkle.

1470
01:22:28,600 --> 01:22:29,700
Closing in on me.

1471
01:22:29,980 --> 01:22:33,020
The air I breathe dissipates before it reaches my lungs.

1472
01:22:33,440 --> 01:22:34,180
I panic.

1473
01:22:34,600 --> 01:22:35,820
There must be a way out.

1474
01:22:36,120 --> 01:22:37,180
It's right there.

1475
01:22:37,580 --> 01:22:38,680
He's right there.

1476
01:22:39,560 --> 01:22:40,700
Swallowing my fears.

1477
01:22:41,000 --> 01:22:42,200
I brandish my pen.

1478
01:22:45,730 --> 01:22:47,130
So, what do you think?

1479
01:22:48,270 --> 01:22:48,870
Uh...

1480
01:22:49,530 --> 01:22:50,690
It's very, uh...

1481
01:22:50,690 --> 01:22:51,250
Freeform.

1482
01:22:51,510 --> 01:22:52,810
If that's what you call it.

1483
01:22:53,510 --> 01:22:56,050
Sorry, I'm not really the right person to ask for feedback.

1484
01:22:57,010 --> 01:22:57,950
Haha, it's okay.

1485
01:22:58,710 --> 01:23:00,970
Yeah, that kind of style has gotten pretty popular nowadays.

1486
01:23:01,870 --> 01:23:05,570
That is, a lot of poems have been putting emphasis on the timing between words and lines.

1487
01:23:06,430 --> 01:23:08,570
When performed out loud, it can be really powerful.

1488
01:23:09,550 --> 01:23:11,510
Was that the inspiration behind this one?

1489
01:23:13,530 --> 01:23:15,170
Well, I'm not sure if I know how to put it.

1490
01:23:15,970 --> 01:23:18,710
I guess you could say that I had some kind of epiphany recently.

1491
01:23:19,550 --> 01:23:21,230
It's been influencing my poems a bit.

1492
01:23:22,230 --> 01:23:23,030
An epiphany?

1493
01:23:23,870 --> 01:23:25,050
Yeah, something like that.

1494
01:23:25,650 --> 01:23:29,330
I'm kind of nervous to talk about deep stuff like that because it's kind of coming on strongly.

1495
01:23:30,410 --> 01:23:32,530
Maybe after everyone is better friends with each other.

1496
01:23:33,290 --> 01:23:33,690
Anyway.

1497
01:23:34,630 --> 01:23:36,210
Here's Monica's writing tip of the day!

1498
01:23:37,250 --> 01:23:41,830
Sometimes, when you're writing a poem or a story, your brain gets too fixated on a specific point.

1499
01:23:42,590 --> 01:23:46,050
If you try so hard to make it perfect, then you'll never make any progress.

1500
01:23:47,130 --> 01:23:50,150
Just force yourself to get something down on the paper and tidy it up later.

1501
01:23:51,010 --> 01:23:52,430
Another way to think about it is this.

1502
01:23:53,170 --> 01:23:57,410
If you keep your pen in the same spot for too long, you just get a big dark puddle of ink.

1503
01:23:58,190 --> 01:23:59,910
So just move your hand and go with the flow.

1504
01:24:00,570 --> 01:24:01,790
That's my advice for today!

1505
01:24:02,570 --> 01:24:03,510
Thanks for listening!

1506
01:24:04,910 --> 01:24:05,690
Oh god.

1507
01:24:07,050 --> 01:24:08,150
Oh, Yuri is here now!

1508
01:24:08,350 --> 01:24:08,530
Right!

1509
01:24:08,870 --> 01:24:09,870
Let's show her our poem.

1510
01:24:10,170 --> 01:24:13,010
This is the person we wrote the poem for in the first place.

1511
01:24:18,440 --> 01:24:21,200
As Yuri reads the poem, I notice her eyes lighten.

1512
01:24:23,600 --> 01:24:24,040
Exceptional.

1513
01:24:25,380 --> 01:24:25,820
Huh?!

1514
01:24:25,820 --> 01:24:28,060
What was that?!

1515
01:24:29,540 --> 01:24:31,120
D-did I say that out loud?

1516
01:24:31,860 --> 01:24:35,760
Yuri first covers her mouth, but then ends up covering her whole face!

1517
01:24:38,360 --> 01:24:38,960
Ooh!

1518
01:24:39,900 --> 01:24:43,000
He's gonna ha- Um...

1519
01:24:43,000 --> 01:24:45,460
You really didn't do anything wrong, Yuri!

1520
01:24:46,640 --> 01:24:46,840
Huh?

1521
01:24:48,260 --> 01:24:48,860
That's...

1522
01:24:48,860 --> 01:24:49,420
I...

1523
01:24:49,860 --> 01:24:50,660
I guess you're right.

1524
01:24:51,420 --> 01:24:53,120
What am I getting so nervous for?

1525
01:24:54,940 --> 01:24:56,340
Yuri takes a breath.

1526
01:24:57,580 --> 01:24:58,140
So...

1527
01:24:58,740 --> 01:25:00,840
What kind of writing experience do you have?

1528
01:25:01,540 --> 01:25:05,420
Your use of imagery and metaphors indicate you've written a lot of poetry before.

1529
01:25:07,000 --> 01:25:07,560
Really?!

1530
01:25:08,220 --> 01:25:08,500
Wow!

1531
01:25:08,780 --> 01:25:11,140
That's a huge compliment coming from you?!

1532
01:25:11,140 --> 01:25:13,140
This is actually my first time!

1533
01:25:14,160 --> 01:25:14,720
Really?!

1534
01:25:14,720 --> 01:25:15,100
Huh?

1535
01:25:15,980 --> 01:25:19,040
Yuri stares at me blankly, then looks at my poem again.

1536
01:25:22,100 --> 01:25:23,220
Well, I know that!

1537
01:25:23,680 --> 01:25:25,420
I just meant, uh...

1538
01:25:26,100 --> 01:25:26,580
Um...

1539
01:25:26,580 --> 01:25:28,800
Yuri trails off, unable to find an excuse.

1540
01:25:29,620 --> 01:25:34,280
She traces her finger along the words in the poem, as if breaking it down more thoroughly.

1541
01:25:36,320 --> 01:25:36,800
Yeah...

1542
01:25:36,800 --> 01:25:37,660
Okay.

1543
01:25:38,860 --> 01:25:40,500
This is the reason I was able to tell.

1544
01:25:41,700 --> 01:25:45,980
It's just that there are specific writing habits that are usually typical of new writers.

1545
01:25:46,660 --> 01:25:50,160
And having been through that myself, I kind of learned to pick up on them.

1546
01:25:50,940 --> 01:25:56,200
I think the most noticeable thing I recognize in new writers is that they try to make their style very deliberate.

1547
01:25:57,160 --> 01:26:01,020
In other words, they tend to pick a writing style separate from the topic matter.

1548
01:26:01,340 --> 01:26:03,140
And they form-fit the two together.

1549
01:26:03,760 --> 01:26:07,140
The end result is that both the style and the expressiveness are weakened.

1550
01:26:08,380 --> 01:26:12,440
Once Yuri finds her train of thought, it's as if her demeanor totally changes.

1551
01:26:13,340 --> 01:26:16,680
Her stammering is completely gone, and she sounds like an expert.

1552
01:26:17,440 --> 01:26:19,240
Of course, that's not something you can be blamed for.

1553
01:26:20,300 --> 01:26:23,800
There are so many different skills and techniques that go into writing even a simple poem.

1554
01:26:25,100 --> 01:26:29,300
Not just finding them and building them, but getting them to work together is probably the most challenging part.

1555
01:26:30,280 --> 01:26:36,340
It might take you some time, but it all comes down with practice, and learning by example, and trying new things.

1556
01:26:37,000 --> 01:26:40,000
I also hope that everyone else in the club gives you valuable feedback.

1557
01:26:41,260 --> 01:26:42,760
Natsuki can be a little bit biased, though.

1558
01:26:45,000 --> 01:26:45,480
Biased?!

1559
01:26:45,480 --> 01:26:45,960
How?!

1560
01:26:48,060 --> 01:26:49,020
Um... well...

1561
01:26:49,020 --> 01:26:49,980
Never mind.

1562
01:26:50,840 --> 01:26:52,860
I shouldn't be talking about people like that.

1563
01:26:53,880 --> 01:26:54,360
Sorry.

1564
01:26:55,620 --> 01:26:56,520
It's fine!

1565
01:26:57,760 --> 01:27:01,760
I'm not sure if Yuri is apologizing to herself, to me, or to Natsuki.

1566
01:27:02,700 --> 01:27:04,860
Do you mind if I read your poem now?

1567
01:27:05,900 --> 01:27:06,660
Please do.

1568
01:27:07,520 --> 01:27:09,760
I'd love to share my thought process behind it.

1569
01:27:10,660 --> 01:27:14,180
Yuri smiles dreamily, as if that's a rare opportunity for her.

1570
01:27:14,940 --> 01:27:16,440
Which itself is kind of funny.

1571
01:27:17,000 --> 01:27:19,380
After all, isn't this supposed to be a literature club?

1572
01:27:20,060 --> 01:27:20,860
Yeah, right?

1573
01:27:22,460 --> 01:27:23,760
Ghost under the light.

1574
01:27:24,620 --> 01:27:27,520
The tendrils of my hair illuminate beneath the amber glow.

1575
01:27:28,100 --> 01:27:28,520
Bathing.

1576
01:27:28,920 --> 01:27:30,160
It must be this one.

1577
01:27:30,400 --> 01:27:33,540
The last remaining street light to have withstood the test of time.

1578
01:27:33,820 --> 01:27:37,800
The last yet to be replaced by the sickening blue-green hue of the future.

1579
01:27:38,320 --> 01:27:39,100
I bathe.

1580
01:27:39,560 --> 01:27:42,440
Calm breathing air of the present, but living in the past.

1581
01:27:42,800 --> 01:27:44,020
The light flickers.

1582
01:27:44,260 --> 01:27:45,300
I flicker back.

1583
01:27:46,020 --> 01:27:47,440
I really like this poem.

1584
01:27:49,940 --> 01:27:50,980
It's a good one.

1585
01:27:52,040 --> 01:27:52,640
I...

1586
01:27:52,640 --> 01:27:55,180
I'm sorry I have such terrible handwriting.

1587
01:27:56,340 --> 01:27:56,940
What?!

1588
01:27:56,940 --> 01:27:59,180
I wasn't thinking that at all!

1589
01:28:00,040 --> 01:28:02,080
But it took you a long time to read.

1590
01:28:03,100 --> 01:28:03,480
Ah!

1591
01:28:04,700 --> 01:28:07,080
Well, I just don't read script very often.

1592
01:28:08,080 --> 01:28:10,280
I actually think your handwriting is pretty!

1593
01:28:11,320 --> 01:28:11,640
Huh?

1594
01:28:12,660 --> 01:28:13,840
That's a relief.

1595
01:28:15,200 --> 01:28:15,820
Also...

1596
01:28:15,820 --> 01:28:17,160
I like the poem!

1597
01:28:19,340 --> 01:28:22,780
Even though it's short, it was really descriptive!

1598
01:28:23,900 --> 01:28:25,220
It wasn't too short.

1599
01:28:25,680 --> 01:28:27,700
I usually write longer poems.

1600
01:28:28,380 --> 01:28:29,740
Not at all!

1601
01:28:30,660 --> 01:28:32,460
I... I'm really glad you like it.

1602
01:28:32,800 --> 01:28:33,700
I'll be honest.

1603
01:28:34,000 --> 01:28:38,040
Since it's our first time sharing, I wanted to write something a little more... mild.

1604
01:28:38,780 --> 01:28:40,760
Something easy to digest, I suppose.

1605
01:28:41,880 --> 01:28:43,920
Are you into ghosts, Yuri?!

1606
01:28:43,920 --> 01:28:44,520
Huhu!

1607
01:28:45,340 --> 01:28:47,580
Actually, the story isn't about a ghost at all, Oliver!

1608
01:28:48,820 --> 01:28:49,300
Really?!

1609
01:28:49,780 --> 01:28:51,760
I must have totally missed the point!

1610
01:28:53,040 --> 01:28:55,800
Well, I suppose you did only glance over it after all.

1611
01:29:07,120 --> 01:29:12,560
But remember that poets often express their own thoughts, feelings, and experiences in their work.

1612
01:29:13,340 --> 01:29:16,400
They usually do more than tell a simple story or paint a picture.

1613
01:29:17,140 --> 01:29:21,900
In this case, perhaps the subject of the poem is only being symbolically compared to a ghost.

1614
01:29:23,160 --> 01:29:29,800
Lingering in her last remaining place of comfort, unable to let go of the past, and soon to be left with nothing.

1615
01:29:30,540 --> 01:29:32,180
That's a lot more solemn!

1616
01:29:32,660 --> 01:29:33,640
Putting it that way?!

1617
01:29:33,640 --> 01:29:35,340
I hadn't even thought of that!

1618
01:29:36,160 --> 01:29:37,300
That's impressive!

1619
01:29:38,240 --> 01:29:38,560
Huh?

1620
01:29:39,320 --> 01:29:41,400
It... it's nothing, really.

1621
01:29:42,560 --> 01:29:44,900
Yours was impressive, too, so...

1622
01:29:44,900 --> 01:29:45,300
Nah!

1623
01:29:45,900 --> 01:29:48,780
If anything, I could probably learn a thing or two from you!

1624
01:29:49,520 --> 01:29:50,580
You think so?

1625
01:29:51,500 --> 01:29:51,820
Yeah!

1626
01:29:52,280 --> 01:29:52,860
Of course!

1627
01:29:54,000 --> 01:29:54,640
Uh...

1628
01:29:54,640 --> 01:29:56,020
You know...

1629
01:29:56,020 --> 01:29:58,540
I was really nervous about doing all this.

1630
01:29:59,280 --> 01:30:00,800
But in the end, I enjoyed it.

1631
01:30:01,580 --> 01:30:03,760
I'm gonna keep doing my best for you, Oliver.

1632
01:30:05,320 --> 01:30:05,860
AHHHHH!

1633
01:30:06,560 --> 01:30:07,420
Me too!

1634
01:30:10,300 --> 01:30:10,840
Whoo!

1635
01:30:11,460 --> 01:30:12,760
I guess that's everyone.

1636
01:30:13,460 --> 01:30:14,900
I glance around the room.

1637
01:30:16,080 --> 01:30:18,260
That was a little more stressful than I anticipated.

1638
01:30:19,400 --> 01:30:23,040
It's as if everyone is judging me for my mediocre writing abilities!

1639
01:30:23,680 --> 01:30:25,000
Wait, something's wrong with the music.

1640
01:30:28,180 --> 01:30:28,860
Or... maybe not.

1641
01:30:29,500 --> 01:30:32,520
Even though they're just being nice, there's no way my poems can stand up to theirs.

1642
01:30:33,360 --> 01:30:35,320
This is a literature club, after all.

1643
01:30:37,380 --> 01:30:37,860
Ahh...

1644
01:30:38,360 --> 01:30:40,740
I guess that's what I ended up getting myself into.

1645
01:30:41,720 --> 01:30:44,300
Across the room, Monica is writing something in her notebook.

1646
01:30:45,340 --> 01:30:47,380
My eyes land on Yuri and Natsuki.

1647
01:30:48,300 --> 01:30:52,400
They gingerly exchange sheets of paper, sharing their respective poems.

1648
01:30:53,300 --> 01:30:56,940
As they read in tandem, I watch each of their expressions change.

1649
