Meanwhile, Yuri smiles sadly.

1651
01:31:03,860 --> 01:31:05,120
What's with this language?

1652
01:31:05,820 --> 01:31:06,380
Huh?

1653
01:31:07,920 --> 01:31:08,480
Um...

1654
01:31:08,480 --> 01:31:09,220
Did you say something?

1655
01:31:09,920 --> 01:31:10,960
Oh, it's nothing.

1656
01:31:12,040 --> 01:31:14,480
Natsuki dismissively returns to the poem...

1657
01:31:14,480 --> 01:31:16,700
Or returns the poem to the desk with one hand.

1658
01:31:18,220 --> 01:31:19,800
I guess you could say it's fancy.

1659
01:31:21,300 --> 01:31:21,860
Ah...

1660
01:31:22,180 --> 01:31:22,460
Thanks.

1661
01:31:23,840 --> 01:31:24,800
Yours is...

1662
01:31:24,800 --> 01:31:25,380
Cute.

1663
01:31:26,380 --> 01:31:26,860
Cute!

1664
01:31:27,700 --> 01:31:29,820
Did you completely miss the symbolism or something?

1665
01:31:30,500 --> 01:31:32,620
It's clearly about the feeling of giving up!

1666
01:31:33,480 --> 01:31:34,580
How could that be cute?

1667
