1678
01:32:00,520 --> 01:32:02,060
Which people did, by the way!

1679
01:32:02,960 --> 01:32:03,880
Monica liked it.

1680
01:32:04,380 --> 01:32:05,460
And Oliver did too!

1681
01:32:06,100 --> 01:32:08,680
So based on that, I'll gladly give you some suggestions of my own.

1682
01:32:09,420 --> 01:32:10,210
First of all...

1683
01:32:11,140 --> 01:32:11,920
Excuse me.

1684
01:32:12,360 --> 01:32:16,180
I appreciate the offer, but I've spent a long time establishing my writing style.

1685
01:32:17,080 --> 01:32:19,080
I don't expect it to change anytime soon.

1686
01:32:19,080 --> 01:32:22,340
Unless, of course, I come across something particularly inspiring.

1687
01:32:23,240 --> 01:32:24,360
Which I haven't yet.

1688
01:32:25,440 --> 01:32:25,800
Mmm!

1689
01:32:26,880 --> 01:32:28,740
And Oliver liked my poem too, you know.

1690
01:32:29,300 --> 01:32:31,260
He even told me he was impressed by it.

1691
01:32:32,500 --> 01:32:33,800
Natsuki suddenly stands up.

1692
01:32:34,820 --> 01:32:35,340
Oh?

1693
01:32:36,360 --> 01:32:40,180
I didn't realize you were so invested in trying to impress our new member, Yuri!

1694
01:32:41,480 --> 01:32:42,000
Huh?

1695
01:32:43,200 --> 01:32:44,260
That's not what I...

1696
01:32:45,840 --> 01:32:46,360
Ooh...

1697
01:32:46,360 --> 01:32:46,880
You're...

1698
01:32:46,880 --> 01:32:48,400
You're just...

1699
01:32:48,400 --> 01:32:49,580
Yuri stands up as well!

1700
01:32:50,900 --> 01:32:54,320
Maybe you're just jealous that Oliver appreciates my advice more than he appreciated yours!

1701
01:32:55,460 --> 01:32:55,980
Huh?!

1702
